    <DataNode elementId="_1-4-alpha-D-galacturonosyl" textLabel="a homogalacturonan" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="60190" dataSource="ChEBI" />
      <Graphics centerX="289.55718994140625" centerY="1089.0087890625" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">|FRAME: 1-4-alpha-D-galacturonosyl &quot;Homogalacturonan&quot;| is a polysaccharide consisting of &amp;alpha;-1,4-linked |FRAME: D-GALACTURONATE| units. It is found in a highly methyl-esterified form when exported into cell walls. |FRAME: 1-4-alpha-D-galacturonosyl &quot;Homogalacturonan&quot;| forms one type of the backbones found in |FRAME: Pectin &quot;pectin&quot;|.</Comment>
